heightened security near baghdad's green  zone it comes after the prime minister's  residence in the fortified area came  under attack  the government says three armored drones  were flown over the compound of mustafa  al-khazami  one hit the building two others were  shut down  to all of those who were worried my  residence was targeted in a cowardly  attack  thanks to god and his grace all of those  working with me and i are doing well  these cowardly rockets and these  cowardly drones do not help in building  nations nor can they be part of any  future  the government said it's investigating  the incident  the u.s state department has offered to  help  in iran the secretary of the supreme  national security council called it a  terrorist attack  he blamed for an intervention for what  he described as new sedition  the attack came two days after  demonstrations against the results of  parliamentary elections in october left  at least one person dead and many  injured  pro-iranian parties lost about  two-thirds of their seats in the vote  they've accused the electoral commission  of rigging the results and demand  recount  many of their supporters are members of  the popular mobilization forces  the party's military wings  they've since occupied areas near the  heavy fortified green zone  that's home to international diplomatic  missions and government offices  pro-iranian groups are among the  demonstrators here but these protesters  deny they carried out the attack and say  it may have been orchestrated by a third  party to ferment violence between them  and security forces  pro-iranian armoured groups have been  accused of carrying out similar drone  attacks over the past two years against  u.s military bases and facilities in the  green zone  some protesters said the drone attack  targeted them and the government  there are evil people behind it who want  to create chaos and divert the public's  attention away from the main cause  demanding justice for those who were  killed on friday and stir animosity  between the government and the popular  mobilization force  some of these protesters are skeptical  they say the attack was fake and accuse  el khazemi of pretending to be a victim  they're vowing to continue their  demonstration  al jazeera  baghdad
 

